The VOPD pairing fix the image's HIP compiler is built with (Dockerfile, stage `llvm`).

VOPDPairingMutation caches each load's transitive load dependencies (LoadPredsCache), and
fuseInstructionPair adds edges after entries were filled, so they go stale. loadsMayOverlap stops
at the first witness while iterating a SmallPtrSet<SUnit *, 8>, whose order past eight entries is
the order of the pointers, so WHICH loads were cached before a fusion depends on heap addresses and
the pair decisions with it: the same source compiles to different code from run to run. A stale
entry can only miss dependencies and so only refuses pairs; dropping the cache after every fusion
makes every answer come from the current DAG.

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/GCNVOPDUtils.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/GCNVOPDUtils.cpp
index 29dec3b8b..b241a2f24 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/GCNVOPDUtils.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/GCNVOPDUtils.cpp
@@ -486,6 +486,8 @@ struct VOPDPairingMutation : ScheduleDAGMutation {
           continue;
 
         if (fuseInstructionPair(*DAG, *ISUI, *JSUI)) {
+          // Fusion adds edges, so cached transitive load dependencies are stale.
+          LoadPredsComputed.reset();
           // Clear to prevent future checks/fusing
           VOPDCapable[JIdx] = false;
           break;
